<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isabel de Clare, 4th Countess of Pembroke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1172">1172</a>–<a href="/years/1220">1220</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isabel de Clare was the daughter and heiress of Richard de Clare, called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke">Strongbow</a>, and Aoife, daughter of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a> of Leinster. Her marriage in 1189 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-marshal-1st-earl-of-pembroke">William Marshal</a> brought him the lordship of Leinster and the earldom of Pembroke. She took an active part in governing her inheritance, and after his death in 1219 she managed her own lands until she died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isabel-de-clare-4th-countess-of-pembroke.jpg" alt="Isabel de Clare, 4th Countess of Pembroke" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sheila1988 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Isabella_Marshal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
